---
title: Ordination of a Deacon: The Presentation
type: prayer
citation: BCP 538
bishop: true
bulletin: full
---

[Rubric] *The bishop and people sit. A Priest and a Lay Person, and additional presenters if desired, standing before the bishop, present the ordinand, saying*
[Presenters] *N.*, Bishop in the Church of God, on behalf of the clergy and people of the Diocese of *N.*, we present to you *N.N.* to be ordained a deacon in Christ's holy catholic Church.
[Bishop] Has *he* been selected in accordance with the canons of this Church? And do you believe *his* manner of life to be suitable to the exercise of this ministry?

---

[Presenters] We certify to you that *he* has satisfied the requirements of the canons, and we believe *him* to be qualified for this order.
[Rubric] *The Bishop says to the ordinand*
[Bishop] Will you be loyal to the doctrine, discipline, and worship of Christ as this Church has received them? And will you, in accordance with the canons of this Church, obey your bishop and other ministers who may have authority over you and your work?

---

[Answer] I am willing and ready to do so; and I solemnly declare that I do believe the Holy Scriptures of the Old and New Testaments to be the Word of God, and to contain all things necessary to salvation; and I do solemnly engage to conform to the doctrine, discipline, and worship of The Episcopal Church.
[Rubric] *The Ordinand then signs the above Declaration in the sight of all present.*
[Rubric] *All stand. The Bishop says to the people*
[Bishop] Dear friends in Christ, you know the importance of this ministry, and the weight of your responsibility in presenting
    *N.N.* for ordination to the sacred order of deacons. Therefore if any of you know any impediment or crime because of which we should not proceed, come forward now, and make it known.
[Rubric] *If no objection is made, the Bishop continues*
[Bishop] Is it your will that *N.* be ordained a deacon?
[Rubric] *The People respond in these or other words*
[People] **It is.**

---

[Bishop] Will you uphold *him* in this ministry?
[Rubric] *The People respond in these or other words*
[People] **We will.**
[Rubric] *The Bishop then calls the people to prayer with these or similar words*
[Bishop] In peace let us pray to the Lord.
